    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked for a new read-only `telephoneDisplay` field: the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans (e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`), while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nTwo edits, following the codebase's existing derived-field pattern:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `getTelephoneDisplay()` derived getter. It strips the leading `+`, resolves the country calling code via the existing `countryCodeOf(...)` helper (reusing the single source of the country-code table), then emits `+<cc> <national digits grouped in threes>`. It defensively returns the telephone unchanged when it's `null`, not E.164, or carries no known country code.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay` `readOnly` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it from `owner.getTelephoneDisplay()` (same mechanism as `displayName`, `initials`, etc.).\n\nThe raw `telephone` remains untouched (still normalized to/stored as E.164).\n\nResults: `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` passes \u2014 `$.telephone` = `+61412345678`, `$.telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678` \u2014 and the full `mvn test` run is `BUILD SUCCESS` with all tests green.",
